# Lab 8: Background Processing
# Create a few tickets first (as dana), and paste their ids below.
@host = https://localhost:7001
@dana = paste-dana-token-here
@alice = paste-alice-token-here
@ticket1 = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@ticket2 = paste-a-ticket-id
@jobId = paste-the-job-id-from-the-202

### Close one ticket, then read its comments: a "closed by" comment from the event handler
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticket2}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{dana}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticket2}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{dana}}

### Bulk close: 202 Accepted right away, with a Location for the job
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/bulk-close
Authorization: Bearer {{dana}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ticketIds": [ "{{ticket1}}", "{{ticket2}}", "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009" ] }

### Follow the job (copy the id from the Location header)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/jobs/{{jobId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{dana}}

### Requesters can't bulk close: 403
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/bulk-close
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ticketIds": [ "{{ticket1}}" ] }

### Take the store down, bulk close, and watch the job retry, then land in dead letters
PUT {{host}}/dev/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "latencyMs": 0, "errorRate": 0, "available": false }

### Jobs that ran out of attempts
GET {{host}}/api/v1/jobs/dead-letters
Authorization: Bearer {{dana}}

### Back to normal
POST {{host}}/dev/chaos/reset

### Urgent and high tickets nobody has picked up (checked every 30 s)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/escalations
Authorization: Bearer {{dana}}
